data.content:
The root cause is that `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 upgraded from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` and all `IOpenApiAny` types removed
Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead:

```csharp
// Before (v1)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (v2)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI v3.1 models nullability via the `type` keyword. `Schema.Type` is now a **flags enum** (`JsonSchemaType`):

```csharp
// Before (v1)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (v2)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;  // remove null
// To ADD nullable: property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityScheme.Reference` / `ReferenceType` restructured
In v2, references no longer use a nested `OpenApiReference` object. The scheme itself carries the `Id`, and you set `Reference` differently:

```csharp
// Before (v1)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After (v2)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";  // shorthand $ref targeting #/components/securitySchemes/oauth2
```

### 4. `OpenApiResponses.TryAdd` — still works but verify the import
`OpenApiResponse` itself is largely unchanged; this line should compile as-is. If you get errors, check that you're referencing `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models` (not the removed `Any` namespace).

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
    oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of namespace changes:**
| v1 (removed) | v2 (replacement) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.OpenApiString` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue.Create()` |
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.OpenApiInteger` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue.Create()` |
| `Schema.Nullable` (bool) | `Schema.Type` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `OpenApiReference.Type = ReferenceType.*` | `schema.Ref = "id"` (string-based `$ref`) |
